From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:44:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] system-linux: report device type without link settings

Report topology before the optional ethtool query so VLAN devices remain
resolvable to their lower devices when firewall4 builds a flowtable.
Refresh the existing local fix for the current netifd source.

Signed-off-by: pbs05 <27010143+pbs05@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/system-linux.c
+++ b/system-linux.c
@@ -3841,6 +3841,8 @@ system_if_dump_info(struct device *dev,
 	void *c, *d;
 	char *s;
 
+	/* Report topology even when a virtual device has no link settings. */
+	system_add_devtype(b, dev->ifname);
 	system_get_ethtool_pause(dev, &rx_pause, &tx_pause, &pause_autoneg);
 
 	memset(&ecmd, 0, sizeof(ecmd));
@@ -3922,8 +3924,6 @@ system_if_dump_info(struct device *dev,
 	blobmsg_add_u8(b, "hw-tc-offload",
 		ethtool_feature_value(dev->ifname, "hw-tc-offload"));
 
-	system_add_devtype(b, dev->ifname);
-
 	/* Add PSE (PoE) status if available */
 	{
 		struct pse_reply_data pse_data;
